    {
      "slug": "portrait-of-abraham-de-potter",
      "title": "Portrait of Abraham de Potter",
      "year": 1649,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Carel_Fabritius_005.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 1937,
      "imageHeight": 2312,
      "story": "Portrait of Abraham de Potter, Amsterdam Silk Merchant is a 1649 portrait painting of silk merchant Abraham de Potter by the Dutch painter Carel Fabritius. The oil painting on canvas is 68.5 by 57 cm. The work has been in the collection of the Rijksmuseum in Amsterdam since 1892.",
      "facts": [
        "At the auction of his estate on 25 June 1892 in London, it was bought by art dealer Martin Henry Colnaghi who sold the portrait to the Rijksmuseum in Amsterdam in the same year.",
        "This portrait and the Self-portrait in the Museum Boijmans Van Beuningen, in Rotterdam, are the only works that have survived from the short period between his collaboration with Rembrandt in Amsterdam and his departure to Delft."
      ],
